---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TableOfContents from '../../components/sections/TableOfContents.astro';

const toc = [
	{ id: 'manual-monitors-ps', label: '1. Manual Monitors (PS Series): Operator Control' },
	{ id: 'auto-tracking-monitors-zdms', label: '2. Auto-Tracking Monitors (ZDMS): Autonomous Response' },
	{ id: 'head-to-head-comparison', label: '3. Head-to-Head Comparison' },
	{ id: 'sizing-and-installation', label: '4. Sizing and Installation Essentials' },
	{ id: 'faq', label: 'Frequently Asked Questions' }
];

const faq = [
	{
		question: 'What is the difference between a manual and an auto-tracking fire water monitor?',
		answer: 'A manual fire water monitor (PS series) is aimed and operated by a firefighter on site, either directly at the turret or via a remote handwheel. An auto-tracking monitor (ZDMS series) continuously scans the protected area with infrared/UV flame detectors and automatically swings onto the fire and suppresses it without operator action — critical for large spaces where a fire must be hit within seconds.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Where are auto-tracking fire cannons (ZDMS) required?',
		answer: 'Auto-tracking cannons are typically specified for large indoor spaces with high ceilings where fire detection and response must be automatic: exhibition halls, atriums, warehouses, aircraft hangars and industrial workshops. The ceiling height and floor area determine the number of cannons and their coverage zones.'
	},
	{
		question: 'What is the effective range of a fire water monitor?',
		answer: 'Effective range depends on flow rate and nozzle configuration. Manual PS monitors commonly deliver 20–60 L/s with ranges of 30–70 metres; auto-tracking ZDMS cannons are typically sized at 20–40 L/s for indoor coverage with response times under 30 seconds. Your fire protection design should size the monitor from the required water density and area of coverage.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Can fire water monitors be used with foam?',
		answer: 'Yes. Most PS series monitors support water or foam spray by switching the nozzle setting, which is why they are common in petrochemical terminals and tank farms. If foam service is planned, specify it in your inquiry so the monitor is configured with the correct foam proportioning interface.'
	}
];

const monitorProducts = [
	{
		slug: 'manual-fire-water-cannon-ps',
		name: 'Manual Fire Water Cannon (PS Series)',
		img: '/assets/products/manual-fire-water-cannon-ps.png',
		desc: 'High-volume manual monitor for water or foam, 30-70 m range'
	},
	{
		slug: 'auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms',
		name: 'Auto-Tracking Jet Suppression Fire Cannon (ZDMS Series)',
		img: '/assets/06_extinguishing_cannons/cannon_p45.png?v=20260729',
		desc: 'IR/UV scanning cannon with autonomous detection and suppression'
	}
];
---

<Layout
	title="Fire Water Monitor Selection: Manual vs Auto-Tracking (ZDMS) Guide"
	description="Fire water monitor guide: manual PS monitors vs auto-tracking ZDMS cannons on range, flow, detection, response time and cost for industrial protection."
	type="article"
	faq={faq}
>
	<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 mb-16">
		<nav class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-6 flex gap-2">
			<a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a>
			<span>/</span>
			<span class="text-gray-600">Guides</span>
		</nav>

		<article class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10">
			<p class="text-brand-red font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-3">Fire Suppression Equipment Guide</p>
			<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">Fire Water Monitor Selection: Manual vs Auto-Tracking (ZDMS)</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">Fire water monitors — also called water cannons — deliver a concentrated, high-volume water stream at range. They come in two fundamentally different operating philosophies: <strong>manual monitors</strong> aimed by operators, and <strong>auto-tracking monitors</strong> that detect, aim and suppress by themselves. Choosing between them is a question of response time, occupancy risk and budget. This guide breaks down the decision.</p>

			<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
				{monitorProducts.map(p => (
					<a href={`/products/${p.slug}/`} class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden hover:border-brand-red hover:shadow-md transition">
						<img src={p.img} alt={p.name} loading="lazy" class="w-full h-40 object-contain bg-white p-3" />
						<div class="p-4">
							<p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-800 group-hover:text-brand-red leading-snug transition-colors">{p.name}</p>
							<p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1 line-clamp-2">{p.desc}</p>
						</div>
					</a>
				))}
			</div>

			
			<TableOfContents headings={toc} />

			<h2 id="manual-monitors-ps" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">1. Manual Monitors (PS Series): Operator Control</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The <a href="/products/manual-fire-water-cannon-ps/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">PS series manual fire water monitor</a> is the workhorse of industrial firefighting: a fixed turret delivering 20–60 L/s at ranges up to 70 metres, switchable between straight jet and spray, and usable with water or foam. Operation is direct (handwheel or turret) or remotely controlled by an operator watching the scene.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Where it belongs:</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-4">
				<li><strong>Petrochemical terminals, tank farms and loading racks</strong> — foam-capable monitors with fixed protection points.</li>
				<li><strong>Outdoor yards and process areas</strong> where operators can safely reach the monitor or a remote control position.</li>
				<li><strong>Cooling and deluge support</strong> where directed manual streams supplement automatic systems.</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The trade-off is simple: a manual monitor is only as fast as its operator. If nobody can safely reach the control point when a fire starts, it may not be fired at all.</p>

			<h2 id="auto-tracking-monitors-zdms" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">2. Auto-Tracking Monitors (ZDMS): Autonomous Response</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The <a href="/products/auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZDMS auto-tracking jet suppression cannon</a> removes the human from the response loop. Dual-band infrared/UV flame detectors scan the protected space continuously; when a flame signature is confirmed, the cannon swings onto the fire, opens the valve and suppresses it — typically within 30 seconds of ignition, around the clock.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Where it belongs:</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-4">
				<li><strong>Large indoor spaces with high ceilings</strong> — exhibition halls, atriums, warehouses, workshops, hangars.</li>
				<li><strong>Occupancies where a fire can grow faster than personnel can respond</strong>.</li>
				<li><strong>Unattended or night-time risk</strong> — the system is always watching.</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Because ZDMS cannons are sized by coverage zone and ceiling height, the design must map detector fields of view and water density across the whole area. This is why the supplier's engineering support matters as much as the hardware.</p>

			<h2 id="head-to-head-comparison" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">3. Head-to-Head Comparison</h2>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 my-5">
				<table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 text-sm">
					<thead class="bg-gray-50">
						<tr>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Criteria</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Manual (PS)</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Auto-Tracking (ZDMS)</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="bg-white divide-y divide-gray-200">
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Response</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Depends on operator reach &amp; reaction</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Autonomous, typically &lt;30 s from ignition</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Flow / range</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">20–60 L/s, 30–70 m</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">20–40 L/s, indoor coverage by zone</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Detection</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">None (operator directed)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Dual-band IR/UV scanning</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Media</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Water or foam (switchable)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Water; foam per configuration</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Typical use</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Tank farms, yards, process areas</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Atriums, warehouses, halls, workshops</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Cost</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Lower hardware cost</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Higher; includes detection &amp; control</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>

			<h2 id="sizing-and-installation" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">4. Sizing and Installation Essentials</h2>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-4">
				<li><strong>Hydraulics first</strong> — the monitor's flow demand (L/s) and required residual pressure must be confirmed against the pump and pipe network before selection.</li>
				<li><strong>Coverage mapping for ZDMS</strong> — detector field of view, ceiling height and water density define cannon count and position; request a layout drawing from the supplier.</li>
				<li><strong>Foam compatibility</strong> — for tank farms, confirm the monitor nozzle and proportioning interface for foam service.</li>
				<li><strong>Testing protocol</strong> — agree a commissioning test (range and response time) with the supplier in the contract.</li>
			</ul>

			<!-- Related guide -->
			<div class="mt-10 bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-black text-gray-900 tracking-tight">Related Guide: The Buying Decision</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Deciding between fixed, remote and smart control — and sizing flow and range for your site? Read the <a href="/guides/fire-water-cannon-buying-guide/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Fire Water Cannon Buying Guide</a>.</p>
			</div>

			<!-- FAQ Section -->
			<h2 id="faq" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-6 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4">
				{faq.map(item => (
					<details class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 p-5 open:border-brand-red/30">
						<summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer list-none">
							<span>{item.question}</span>
							<span class="text-brand-blue text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
						</summary>
						<p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-sm">{item.answer}</p>
					</details>
				))}
			</div>

			<!-- CTA -->
			<div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
				<div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-blue to-blue-800 px-6 sm:px-10 py-10 text-center">
					<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">Sizing a Monitor System for Your Site?</h2>
					<p class="mt-3 text-blue-100 max-w-xl mx-auto text-sm leading-relaxed">Send your site type, protected area and ceiling height — our engineers respond with cannon layout and pricing within 12 hours.</p>
					<div class="mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-center gap-4">
						<a href="/contact/?product=Fire%20Water%20Monitor" class="px-8 py-4 bg-brand-red text-white font-bold rounded-lg hover:opacity-90 transition">Request a Quote</a>
						<a href="https://wa.me/8618684324501?text=Hi%2C%20I%20need%20help%20sizing%20fire%20water%20monitors" class="px-8 py-4 bg-white text-brand-blue font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-50 transition" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
